in Governance
A good system of governance requires three separate branches of
government: the legislature, the executive, and the judiciary. These
branches work together, but each has its own distinct role.
The separation of powers creates a system of checks and balances. This
ensures that no single branch can become too powerful.
If one branch oversteps its authority, the others can step in to restore
balance.
