Many institutions in India have mottos that are inspired by
the wisdom found in ancient texts.
The motto of the Government of India is &quot;Satyameva Jayate,&quot;
which translates to &quot;Truth alone triumphs.&quot; This reflects the
importance of truth in governance.
The Supreme Court of India has the motto &quot;Yato
Dharmastato Jayah,&quot; meaning &quot;Where there is dharma, there
is victory.&quot; This emphasizes the role of dharma, or
righteousness, in achieving success.
