provides support to local
governments.
Central Government
Takes charge of nationwide problems and ensures the overall
functioning of the country.
 </span></div></li><li class="transcript-item-module__V3aA8a__root"><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__medium">7. </span><div><a class="link link-module__Gim9xG__root link-module__Gim9xG__primary weight-regular link-module__Gim9xG__large link-module__Gim9xG__underline" aria-label="Slide 7: Inspirations from Ancient" href="https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/chapter-notes-governance-6th-class-new-socialpdf/274079643#7">Inspirations from Ancient</a><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__small">Texts in
Institutional Mottos
Many institutions in India have mottos that are inspired by
the wisdom found in ancient texts.
The motto of the Government of India is "Satyameva Jayate,"
which translates to "Truth alone triumphs." This reflects the
importance of truth in governance.
The Supreme Court of India has the motto "Yato
Dharmastato Jayah," meaning "Where there is dharma, there
is victory." This emphasizes the role of dharma, or
righteousness, in achieving success.
 </span></div></li><li class="transcript-item-module__V3aA8a__root"><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__medium">8. </span><div><a class="link link-module__Gim9xG__root link-module__Gim9xG__primary weight-regular link-module__Gim9xG__large link-module__Gim9xG__underline" aria-label="Slide 8: Dr. A.P.J. Abdul" href="https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/chapter-notes-governance-6th-class-new-socialpdf/274079643#8">Dr. A.P.J. Abdul</a><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__small">Kalam
Missile Man of India
Dr. Kalam was a renowned scientist, known for his contributions to India's
space and missile programs.
11th President of India
He served as the President of India from 2002 to 2007.
Education and Innovation
Dr. Kalam was passionate about education and encouraged young Indians
to pursue their dreams.
 </span></div></li><li class="transcript-item-module__V3aA8a__root"><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__medium">9. </span><div><a class="link link-module__Gim9xG__root link-module__Gim9xG__primary weight-regular link-module__Gim9xG__large link-module__Gim9xG__underline" aria-label="Slide 9: Understanding Democracy
People's Rule
Democracy" href="https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/chapter-notes-governance-6th-class-new-socialpdf/274079643#9">Understanding Democracy
People's Rule
Democracy</a><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__small">is a system where representatives make
decisions on behalf of the citizens.
The term 'democracy' comes from Greek words: 'demos'
meaning 'people' and 'kratos' meaning 'rule' or 'power'.
Direct Democracy Example
Imagine a class deciding on a picnic spot. Everyone discusses
options, but it's hard to agree.
The teacher suggests voting. Each student raises their hand
for their preferred spot, and the one with the most votes
wins.
 </span></div></li><li class="transcript-item-module__V3aA8a__root"><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__medium">10. </span><div><a class="link link-module__Gim9xG__root link-module__Gim9xG__primary weight-regular link-module__Gim9xG__large link-module__Gim9xG__underline" aria-label="Slide 10: Features of Indian" href="https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/chapter-notes-governance-6th-class-new-socialpdf/274079643#10">Features of Indian</a><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__small">Democracy
Representative
Democracy
Citizens elect
representatives to make
decisions on their behalf.
Largest
Democracy
India is the world's largest
democracy with around 970
million voters.
Universal
Suffrage
All Indian citizens above the
age of 18 have the right to
vote.
Grassroots
Democracy
India's system encourages
citizen participation in
decisions that affect them.
 </span></div></li><li class="transcript-item-module__V3aA8a__root"><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__medium">11. </span><div><a class="link link-module__Gim9xG__root link-module__Gim9xG__primary weight-regular link-module__Gim9xG__large link-module__Gim9xG__underline" aria-label="Slide 11: Conclusion
Governance and government" href="https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/chapter-notes-governance-6th-class-new-socialpdf/274079643#11">Conclusion
Governance and government</a><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__small">are essential for maintaining order and
harmony in society.
Democracy allows us to have a say in how we are governed, ensuring that
everyone's voice matters.
 </span></div></li><li class="transcript-item-module__V3aA8a__root"><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__medium">12. </span><div><a class="link link-module__Gim9xG__root link-module__Gim9xG__primary weight-regular link-module__Gim9xG__large link-module__Gim9xG__underline" aria-label="Slide 12: Key Terms
House
An assembly" href="https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/chapter-notes-governance-6th-class-new-socialpdf/274079643#12">Key Terms
House
An assembly</a><span class="text Text-module__DjdFRa__root weight-regular Text-module__DjdFRa__small">where laws are
discussed or passed.
Nominal
In name only, meaning the
President of India and the
Governor of a State are not the
actual executive heads.
 </span></div></li></ul></div></div></div><dialog class="modal Modal-module__WM7rSG__root Modal-module__WM7rSG__medium" id="_r_2_" aria-labelledby="_r_2_-title"></dialog><div class="actions-menu-container actions-menu-module__Av7kDa__root" data-cy="actions-menu-mobile"><div class="hide-scrollbar ActionsMenuTopBar-module__VmiVHq__root"><div class="ActionsMenuTopBar-module__VmiVHq__scroller"><button type="button" class="button Button-module__4HgN-q__root Button-module__4HgN-q__secondary Button-module__4HgN-q__outlined Button-module__4HgN-q__small Button-module__4HgN-q__fullWidth"><span><span class="Button-module__4HgN-q__iconSlot"><span class="Button-module__4HgN-q__iconEl"><span role="img" aria-label="info-new icon" class="icon Icon-module__J9mFQG__icon Icon-module__J9mFQG__mask" style="--size: 16px; --icon: url(/images/next/svg/info-new.svg?v=undefined);"></span></span><span class="Button-module__4HgN-q__spinnerEl"><svg class="spinner" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 50 50" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" data-dd-excluded-activity-mutations="true"><path d="M43.935,25.145c0-10.318-8.364-18.683-18.683-18.683c-10.318,0-18.683,8.365-18.683,18.683h4.068c0-8.071,6.543-14.615,14.615-14.615c8.072,0,14.615,6.543,14.615,14.615H43.935z"><animateTransform attributeType="xml" attributeName="transform" type="rotate" from="0 25 25" to="360 25 25" dur="0.6s" repeatCount="indefinite"></animateTransform></path></svg></span></span><span class="ellipsis">Overview</span></span></button><button type="button" class="button Button-module__4HgN-q__root Button-module__4HgN-q__secondary Button-module__4HgN-q__outlined Button-module__4HgN-q__small Button-module__4HgN-q__fullWidth"><span><span class="Button-module__4HgN-q__iconSlot"><span class="Button-module__4HgN-q__iconEl"><span role="img" aria-label="layout-list icon" class="icon Icon-module__J9mFQG__icon Icon-module__J9mFQG__mask" style="--size: 16px; --icon: url(/images/next/svg/layout-list.svg?v=undefined);"></